#hasheq((content-digest . "fcf477093908c08c36ddedd9ae3961dbbf07cfec683174d457d45e4018c0acdc") (report . "Two review rounds. (1) 3c37f443 -> APPROVED with four non-blocking findings; three were acted on before the next head: the wave contract's literal --check mode is now delivered as the check subcommand (a fail-closed alias of verify listed in the usage text and pinned by a new both-directions test, closing the dead --check parse the round flagged); a duplicated require block in the CLI test was merged; and the report documents the two dispositioned observations - refusal verdicts deliberately exit 0 with typed codes on stdout (nonzero exit is reserved for tool failure, consumers parse stdout, recorded as an F8-adjacent ergonomics note) and the binding-time review() reconciliation in scripts/gsd-delivery.py that accepts a reviewed-sha which is an evidence-only ancestor of the receipt head, which is what allows a pre-merge reviewed head to be bound to the post-merge receipt and stays fail-closed through require_receipt_tip on any non-evidence drift. (2) 220f676b (this head) -> APPROVED: the delta was exactly the three fixes and the report update, the round-1 substance was re-verified intact (typed verdicts, hermetic git subprocesses, exclusion contract, gate refusals, purity wiring, register guards pinned to exactly F1-F4), and the three remaining observations (exit-0 ergonomics, no production caller yet passes --receipt-head because production head binding is enforced by the coordinator/expected-head path the wave contract explicitly permits, and record-commit-purity scanning only commits that touch the evidence record directory) are recorded as informational with the report carrying the same statements, not smoothed over. The reviewer verified the F2 exclusion contract is byte-identical to the Python digest contract and that the empty-tree property reproduces the W1 publication range through the new tool. (3) Round 3, delta review after the round-2 approved head: the repository lint-quality gate surfaced two defects the quick pre-commit lane does not check (it verifies raco-fmt canonicality but not the 150-column width): two 151-character usage lines in scripts/gsd-evidence-bind.rkt, and the register fixture reflow had moved the README test-lines metric by one without a resync. Both repaired (usage reflowed with identical flags and subcommands, the 7 CLI tests still green; README resynced by scripts/metrics.rkt --sync-all), which moved the content head to 4e0c3cf1 and the computed digest to 85b41b42. Per the content-change rule this triggered a fresh delta round: the reviewer correctly required the trio to be rebound at the exact head (the round-2-bound records would have failed verify with digest-mismatch at 4e0c3cf1 - the F2 shape on our own branch), required the test-lines drift to be named (it is the register fixture's format-string reflow in tests/test-wave-delivery-integrity-register.rkt), and required fresh fast-suite provenance because the delta touches a .rkt test file. All three are done: the digest was recomputed by gsd-evidence-bind.rkt digest at 4e0c3cf1 over base 69647f1c, the records are rebound to the new head and digest, and the fast suite was re-executed at this head with the RUN-SUMMARY re-stamped under artifacts/wave-delivery-integrity/v1.00.31-w2/.") (reviewed-sha . "a1a85bdc1907bd175a4b81fcdddc60346e257038") (reviewer . "independent read-only reviewer subagents (fresh non-author, reviewer role, model deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash; two rounds, a new session per round)") (scope . "full implementation diff main (69647f1ce5d36798e790b1d62a3b79c62b8b011f) ... head 220f676b9a1dc4619aa367da811ce4e8cb2205b1 for v1.00.31 W2 evidence identity and digest integrity (register F2/F3/F4 plus the F12 sentinel close-out): scripts/gsd-evidence-bind.rkt (new tool: digest/verify/bind/record-commit with typed verdicts digest-ok/digest-mismatch/malformed-digest/pure/impure-record-commit, the check alias of verify demanded lit